{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>These are the numbered of the children of Israel</b> etc. This count is smaller than the count in the Wilderness of Sinai by one thousand eight hundred and twenty. For had there been more here, they would now say: we are numerous enough to conquer the land; but had they been fewer, they would say: we cannot conquer it. Therefore HaShem did not want this count to exceed that of the Wilderness of Sinai, since even so they conquered it, for there is no restraint for YHWH to deliver, whether with many or with few."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:51.822187457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}